<urn:atm:triage:finding/BOUNDARYTEST-001-AL5>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BOUNDARYTEST-001-AL5" ;
  triage:title "al5_uds_is_a_framework_adapter_over_the_one_client_and_router fails on integrate/phase-al base (stale test assertion)" ;
  triage:description "The boundary_enforcement test asserts combined.contains(\"PrivateStagingDirectory::create(parent)\"). PrivateStagingDirectory::create still exists in crates/atm-http-runtime/src/unix_socket.rs, but its signature gained an owner_uid parameter (now PrivateStagingDirectory::create(parent, socket.owner_uid.get())), which internally delegates to the shared private_staging::allocate(parent, \"uds\", ...) helper checked by a separate assertion in the same test. The single-arg exact-string assertion was never updated after the owner_uid parameter was added, so it can no longer match. Independently reproduced by team-lead and quality-mgr on integrate/phase-al HEAD 4fda46f9 in a clean detached worktree via 'cargo test -p atm-architecture --test boundary_enforcement al5_uds_is_a_framework_adapter_over_the_one_client_and_router', with zero PR #820 changes applied. Confirmed PR #820's diff touches zero files under crates/atm-http-runtime/ or crates/atm-architecture/, so it is not the cause. Fix must update/remove the stale exact-string assertion to match the current PrivateStagingDirectory::create(parent, owner_uid) signature, not revert or rename production code." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-al" ;
